WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.537
Step five breaks the seal on purpose.

2
00:00:02.537 --> 00:00:04.401
Add one line, the word edited,

3
00:00:04.401 --> 00:00:08.613
to the register file inside the
sealed package, and check again.

4
00:00:08.613 --> 00:00:11.026
Two checks fail, and each says why.

5
00:00:11.026 --> 00:00:13.772
The sums check fails
because the register file

6
00:00:13.772 --> 00:00:16.238
no longer matches its
hash in the sums file.

7
00:00:16.238 --> 00:00:20.900
The chain check fails because the file no
longer matches the hash its record holds.

8
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.375
That's the point of sealing.

9
00:00:22.375 --> 00:00:25.901
Months later, an assessor can
show that the files are the ones

10
00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:29.075
the tool and the kit wrote, or
see exactly which one isn't.

11
00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:31.900
Step six cleans up: delete the out folder.

12
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.203
In a real program, the sealed folder
lives in the evidence repository,

13
00:00:36.203 --> 00:00:39.650
and retention follows the
records officer's schedule.
